    <title>Constructor and Destructor</title>
    <sectiondef kind="func">
      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__network__creation_1gaceb794444113eebd20d8a6fabdc2e2f9" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type><ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref> *</type>
        <definition>NDXLNetwork * ndxlCreateNetwork</definition>
        <argsstring>(void *_Params)</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlCreateNetwork</name>
        <param>
          <type>void *</type>
          <declname>_Params</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Creates an empty <ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref> object and returns a pointer to it. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Params</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to extra memory used by the network. May be NULL.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If successful, returns a new <ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref> pointer, otherwise returns NULL.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>The local simulation time of a newly created network is always initialised 0, and only updates on a successful integration step.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>NDXL stores the supplied <computeroutput>void* _Params</computeroutput> pointer without copying the associated data or managing its lifetime. The pointed-to memory must remain valid for as long as the network uses it. The user remains responsible for managing any allocations.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__network__creation_1ga41c3dace543bac6ff2d0597bd5cb03e1" kindref="member">ndxlDestroyNetwork</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
