      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__network__creation_1ga41c3dace543bac6ff2d0597bd5cb03e1" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>const int</type>
        <definition>const int ndxlDestroyNetwork</definition>
        <argsstring>(NDXLNetwork **_Network)</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlDestroyNetwork</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref> **</type>
          <declname>_Network</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Destroys a network created using <ref refid="group__network__creation_1gaceb794444113eebd20d8a6fabdc2e2f9" kindref="member">ndxlCreateNetwork()</ref>, and zeroes the pointer. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">_Network</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to <ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref> pointer.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If _Network or *_Network are NULL, returns <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gae9261a8e1c9a6cebdc947ee5798cca1e" kindref="member">NDXL_ERR</ref>, otherwise zeroes *_Network, and returns NDXL_OK.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>The network pointer is zeroed after the associated memory is freed, so that subsequent operations using the pointer variable passed to this function can detect that the network has been destroyed.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>Destroying a network also destroys all vertices, edges, and noise channels owned by that network. All pointers to the network and its owned objects become invalid. The memory associated with the relevant objects&apos; user-defined <computeroutput>void* _Params</computeroutput> pointers is not handled by the destructors, and must be managed explicitly by the user.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>Only the pointer variable passed to this function is zeroed. Any other pointers referencing the destroyed network become invalid and must not be used.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Errors raised</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Network is NULL.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gafa88b2be61049bce770f14eeac651348" kindref="member">NDXL_VALUE_ERR</ref> : *_Network is NULL.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__network__creation_1gaceb794444113eebd20d8a6fabdc2e2f9" kindref="member">ndxlCreateNetwork</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
